          "text": "{\"body\":\"## Summary / 概要\\r\\n\\r\\nFixed two bugs that occurred when using the `useAI` hook on the `_debug` page.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Bug 1: Infinite Loop (Maximum update depth exceeded)\\r\\n\\r\\n**Root Cause:**  \\r\\nThe `useAI` hook internally includes `options.tools` and `options.suggestions` in the `useEffect` dependency array ([useAI.ts:186](https://github.com/meetsmore/meetsone/blob/master/node_modules/.pnpm/@meetsmore+use-ai-client@0.1.4_@types+react@18.0.26_react@18.3.1/node_modules/@meetsmore/use-ai-client/src/useAI.ts#L186)):\\r\\n\\r\\n```typescript\\r\\n// Inside useAI.ts\\r\\nuseEffect(() => {\\r\\n  // tools registration logic\\r\\n}, [enabled, options.tools, options.id, options.invisible, registerTools, unregisterTools, waitForRender]);\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nIn the original code, `tools` and `suggestions` were defined inline within the component, creating new object/array references on every render:\\r\\n\\r\\n```typescript\\r\\n// Before - new references created on every render\\r\\nuseAI({\\r\\n  tools: { getWeather },  // ← new object\\r\\n  suggestions: ['今日の天気はなんですか？'],  // ← new array\\r\\n})\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThis caused: `useEffect` detects change → state update → re-render → new reference → `useEffect` detects change... creating an infinite loop.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Fix:**  \\r\\nDefined `tools` and `suggestions` outside the component to stabilize references.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Bug 2: Tool Execution Hang (stuck at \\\"waiting for render...\\\")\\r\\n\\r\\n**Root Cause:**  \\r\\nThe `useAI` hook has a mechanism to wait for React re-renders after tool execution before sending the response ([useAI.ts:155-160](https://github.com/meetsmore/meetsone/blob/master/node_modules/.pnpm/@meetsmore+use-ai-client@0.1.4_@types+react@18.0.26_react@18.3.1/node_modules/@meetsmore/use-ai-client/src/useAI.ts#L155-L160)):\\r\\n\\r\\n```typescript\\r\\n// Inside useAI.ts\\r\\nconst waitForRender = useCallback(() => {\\r\\n  return new Promise<void>(resolve => {\\r\\n    renderResolvers.current.push(resolve);  // resolves on next render\\r\\n  });\\r\\n}, []);\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThis Promise resolves on the next render, but since the `DebugPage` component has no state changes after tool execution, no re-render occurs, leaving the Promise unresolved indefinitely.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Fix:**  \\r\\nAdded `invisible: true` option. This option is designed for components without UI state changes, skipping the render wait.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Notion Ticket\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- Replace link with Actual Ticket -->\\r\\nhttps://www.notion.so/meetsmore/TS-9882\\r\\n\\r\\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria checked\\r\\n\\r\\n## 🤖 How is AI used? / AI の使用方法\\r\\n\\r\\nUsed Claude Code for bug investigation and fix implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Screenshots / スクリーンショット\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] No design change / デザイン変更なし\\r\\n\\r\\n<table><tr><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr>\\r\\n<tr><td>\\r\\n<!-- Before Image here / ここに修正前 -->\\r\\n\\r\\n</td><td>\\r\\n<!-- After Image here / ここに修正後 -->\\r\\n\\r\\n</td></tr>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n\\r\\n## Checklist / チェックリスト\\r\\n\\r\\n>[!NOTE]\\r\\n> **How to use**:\\r\\n> - Every item should be checked **or** have an explanation as to why.\\r\\n> - If an item is not applicable, check it.\\r\\n> - e.g: You did not add a new dependency, you still check '[x] Any added dependencies are up-to-date.'\\r\\n\\r\\n🚨 **This section MUST be filled out.**\\r\\n💁🏼‍♂️ **This section must be filled out by a human engineer.**\\r\\n🤖 **AI cannot fill out this section.**\\r\\n📝 **If your PR is trivial (e.g. just changing config or README), you can skip.**\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] My pull request is simple, and does not need the quality checklist.\\r\\n\\r\\n**OR**\\r\\n\\r\\n- [ ]  Code has enough test coverage *for the amount of risk*.\\r\\n- [ ]  Code has JSDoc.\\r\\n- [ ]  Documentation is sufficient (can you understand it without context?).\\r\\n- [ ]  No secrets, API keys, tokens, are hardcoded in the code.\\r\\n- [ ]  Third party APIs integrat